NETWORK_SETUP_HTML = r'''
<section class="network-setup" aria-labelledby="network-setup-title"><header><p class="eyebrow">LOCAL DEVICE DISCOVERY</p><h3 id="network-setup-title" tabindex="-1">Choose the networks to discover</h3></header><p>The HUD reads this PC's interfaces, routes and neighbor cache automatically. Optional Nmap host discovery refreshes your selected private networks every 15 minutes.</p><form id="network-setup-form"><label class="network-enable"><input type="checkbox" id="network-enabled"> Discover devices in the selected scopes</label><label for="network-scopes">Private on-link scopes <small>One CIDR per line; up to 4,096 addresses combined.</small></label><textarea id="network-scopes" rows="3" maxlength="4096" spellcheck="false" placeholder="Choose an available scope below"></textarea><div id="network-available" class="network-available" aria-label="Available private discovery scopes"><p>Reading available interfaces…</p></div><p class="network-note">IPv4 scopes are split into batches of at most 256 addresses. IPv6 discovery accepts known individual /128 peers; it never sweeps an IPv6 subnet. These checks use your existing permissions. Some devices ignore discovery; their absence does not prove they are offline.</p><details><summary>See traffic from other devices</summary><p>A switched or Wi-Fi network normally exposes this PC’s own traffic and local broadcasts. Discovering an address does not reveal all of its traffic. Use a router flow export, a mirrored switch port covering those devices, or an endpoint sensor to expand coverage. A capture outside a NAT router usually loses individual private-device identity.</p><p>Google Wifi’s local status page supplies router health. Its connected-device usage view lives in Google Home; no device-traffic connector is configured here. A detected DNS, TLS, HTTP or other protocol is evidence of a service exchange, not proof of the application running on a device. Encrypted content remains unreadable.</p></details><button id="network-save" type="submit" disabled>Save discovery settings</button><p id="network-setup-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Loading saved discovery settings…</p></form></section>
'''

